{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30315 - PROTEIN:5777",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SF-188 through a series of molecular interactions. The compound directly targets CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, an enzyme involved in sialylation, a process critical for cell surface glycosylation. This enzyme is subsequently targeted by (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol, which in turn has SF-188 as its target. Additionally, Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool is also linked to 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, which targets SF-188, and to Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate, which also has SF-188 as its target. These findings suggest that Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool may influence SF-188 through a complex network of enzymatic interactions, potentially affecting cellular processes involving sialylation and metabolic pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's role in modulating biological functions through indirect mechanisms, emphasizing its potential as a therapeutic agent.",
